With this helper a missing or renamed cassette makes the test skip silently in CI instead of failing. The other tests here use `@pytest.mark.vcr()`, which resolves the same `{node.name}.yaml` cassette and fails when it's missing. How about using that on both sync/async tests and dropping this helper and the manual `vcr.use_cassette` block?

```python
@pytest.mark.vcr()
@pytest.mark.skipif(...)
def test_responses_create_captures_computer_tool_loop(
    span_exporter, openai_client, instrument_with_content
):
    _skip_if_not_latest()
    history = [...]
    first_response = openai_client.responses.create(...)
    ...
```
